  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe ongoing weather pattern is as uneventful as it gets for our\nregion and for the most part, a persistence forecast was used. \nIn fact, with a very similar setup to last night, tonight's \nforecast low temperatures were mostly copied over from last \nnight's observed lows with a few minor tweaks around the Lake \nPlain.\n\nA moisture-starved cold front will move through the area on\nThursday, but precipitation is not expected from this front. The\nonly visible impact from this front will be partly sunny to \nmostly cloudy skies Thursday instead of the abundant sunshine we\nhave seen the last several days, followed by slightly cooler \ntemperatures and a return to abundant sunshine on Friday.\n\nAnother weak cold front will move through the area during the\nMonday/Tuesday timeframe next week, but chances are that this\nwill also be moisture-starved with little to no precipitation.",
